    <html:p>
  We might want this app to also render a forest synced with a git
  repo or served over the internet. The web interface is already good,
  so we could effectively just wrap a browser to handle the rendering.
  Or maybe even easier, we can use tailscale to have a synced private
  forest accessible from mobile
</html:p>
    <html:p>
  Cancelled: iCloud sync covers mobile. The AppleScript-based sync in
  <fr:link href="/sss-003M/" title="Syncing with Apple Reminders" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-003M/" display-uri="sss-003M" type="local">Syncing with Apple Reminders</fr:link> creates items in native Reminders and Calendar apps, which
  automatically appear on iPhone/iPad/Apple Watch. Siri can add reminders
  to the "Forester" list, and pull syncs them back into the forest.
</html:p>
